Independent QA: **changes-required** for this bounded SQL checkpoint.

**F1 (P2): an empty SSL override disables TLS in Prisma CLI.** At `backend/src/config/databaseUtils.ts:185`, `DB_SSLMODE=""` rewrites an explicit `DATABASE_URL?...sslmode=verify-full` to `sslmode=disable`. The parent CLI preserved that direct URL. With `PGSSLMODE=verify-full`, an unconnected real pg Client still resolves runtime SSL to `true`, while CLI receives `disable`. This can cause plaintext administrative connections or TLS-required connection failures. Reject ambiguous blank input or preserve the explicit secure mode consistently; add blank/whitespace regression cases through runtime and actual Prisma configuration loading. No database was contacted.

Focused tests: **34/34 pass** after credential-free Prisma generation; schema validation and exact baseline/final evidence reproduction pass. Current CI: all five workflows pass, including **759 backend tests** and production startup/readiness. Complete published scope is **two linear commits, eight files, +390/-86**, all within SQL configuration/tests/maintained documentation/required image packaging. Bot review was refused solely for code-review quota; no bot completion is claimed.

The issue and PR explain the base-state problem and partial outcome clearly. Full Firebase/GCP work remains unfinished. Route F1 to the existing owner and retain readiness withholding; no merge or readiness approval is given.

Synthetic reproduction from `backend` (unconnected Client only):
```js
const { resolveDatabaseConnection } = require("./src/config/databaseUtils");
const { Client } = require("pg");
process.env.PGSSLMODE = "verify-full";
const c = resolveDatabaseConnection({
  DATABASE_URL: "postgresql://synthetic:synthetic@localhost/app?sslmode=verify-full",
  DB_SSLMODE: ""
});
console.log(new Client(c.poolConfig).connectionParameters.ssl,
  new URL(c.url).searchParams.get("sslmode"));
// observed: true, disable
```

